# graphify state, if anyone builds a graph over this repo. It is generated,
# machine-specific (upstream warns its branch.json, worktree.json,
# needs_update and cache/ must never be committed), and can be large. This
# repo ships graphify as an mcp-servers/ manifest only - it never builds or
# commits a graph. tests/smoke-mcp.sh reads .graphify/graph.json as a
# precondition, so an ignored-but-present directory is the expected state
# for anyone who wants that server smoke-tested for real.
.graphify/

# Claude Code's in-repo directory. Every path it holds is either
# machine-specific or an emission whose source is tracked elsewhere, so none
# of it belongs in this repo's history: settings.json carries absolute
# /mnt/c/... paths and per-session permission grants; .claude/skills/ and
# .claude/agents/ were rejected outright when S7 was planned, as a
# self-referential fourth copy competing with the validated install path;
# and .claude/workflows/ is where the unattended-run binding is *emitted*,
# its source being skills/unattended-ops/templates/bindings/claude-code/
# (ADR-0018's one-source-per-client-emission shape, applied here too).
.claude/
